GLORB Colorwaves, Hiphotic, Frizzles, Black Hole, Tartan -- original-code renderer comparison
Date: 2026-11-14
Source: tycwled c54b327 (glorb_fx.cpp SHA256 d8eb83977ba381d4b099f866494e492f4e4d1a54e87068d4ca7fb2d97b4b7581)
Status: all ten cases (five effects x sound option off/on) equal over 4201 frames

Method
  Original: the effect function and the WLED helper closure it calls (palette, blend, add, fade,
  blur, ledmap, BusManager) execute from the GLORB.1.3 debug application, SHA256
  888454572bc34beb86e1595e86aef3ff9f477e2f6501201011e91279f29c597a, in Ghidra 12.0.4's P-code
  emulator (Xtensa windowed ABI) against an authored memory bus. Segment fields, the 48-byte
  palette, the clock and processed volume are written by the harness: a diagnostic boundary, not
  the firmware running as shipped.
  Candidate: glorb_fx.cpp compiled on the host against a boundary that follows WLED v16.0.1 for
  every WLED call the usermod makes: color_add (colors.cpp), addPixelColorXY with its default
  preserveCR, the raw segment buffer accessors, setPixelColor, fill, the default-palette branch of
  color_from_palette, getMappedPixelIndex/getLengthTotal. Header SHA256
  9a270fc53b567c0ccd421b729bdcc66495307d6821f9a5317580abadca5979cf, driver
  24b91fe59a23c2ac4b95b9ed148ef73e65b918042d1e83c0256d06f6471f66f9, binary
  0c0e51b193938dc0240a0ced7427538975ffc543c96c80a47d5e4278de01d1f5. The host used for the
  September and early November checks modelled WLED 0.14 there and matched; it could not see the
  add defect below.
  Inputs: factory presets 1, 2, 7, 11, 12 (palettes 18, 34, 18, 13, 59), 20x6 logical cells,
  factory ledmap with 40 holes, 120-pixel bus. Long input: 4201 frames, 42 Hz rounded to whole
  milliseconds, through 100.000 s; processed volume 0, 1.5, 64, 1023.75, 512.5, 0 in 700-frame
  blocks (trace SHA256 38785b34024b86c911ab01195f03b3f3a7044620c92ba7f800103bc25aa0808f, the same
  input as the Running cases). Sound option on sets check1; Hiphotic, Frizzles, Black Hole and
  Tartan have no sound option and never read check1 or audio in the original.
  Compared: every logical and mapped RGB byte and the 12 segment-state bytes (step, call, aux0,
  aux1) of every frame, no tolerance. Control per case: one flipped bit in the mapped bus of
  frame 2100 of the host capture is rejected at that frame. Each original capture is sealed by
  the runner (status complete); the last eight ran from read-only per-job snapshots of runtime,
  assets and input whose manifests were unchanged afterwards.

Results (head c54b327; "before" = 92e8321, the source before this branch)
